  "result": "{\"seen_before\": true, \"matches\": [\"PowerToys#45987\", \"PowerToys#42192\", \"PowerToys#40247\"], \"answer\": \"This request has been made before. Earlier tickets asking for a real-time network speed indicator on the taskbar were closed as duplicates of the main tracking issue #8756 (older ones point to #828), so add your 👍 and any extra detail there. The maintainers said in #45987 that PowerToys can't customise the Windows taskbar directly because the APIs to do so are private. They suggested posting the request in the Windows Feedback Hub (WinKey+F). They also pointed to the concepts in #45201, which show network monitoring in the Command Palette Dock, as an alternative that isn't on the taskbar. Until Windows exposes a way to do this, third-party tools such as NetSpeedMonitor or TrafficMonitor are the workaround.\"}",
